== Usage ==
* Maintain [[gww:Essence Bond|Essence Bond]].
* Bonder 1 maintains [[gww:Blessed Aura|Blessed Aura]] on themselves, and [[gww:Retribution|Retribution]] and [[gww:Strength of Honor|Strength of Honor]] on you.
* Bonder 2 maintains [[gww:Blessed Aura|Blessed Aura]] on themselves, [[gww:Life Attunement|Life Attunement]] on Bonder 1, and [[gww:Essence Bond|Essence Bond]] and [[gww:Balthazar's Spirit|Balthazar's Spirit]] on you.
* Have your bonders cast [[gww:Holy Wrath|Holy Wrath]], [[gww:Judge's Insight|Judge's Insight]], [[gww:Shield of Judgment|Shield of Judgment]], [[gww:Splinter Weapon|Splinter Weapon]], and [[gww:Spell Breaker|Spell Breaker]] on you prior to engaging groups.
* Maintain [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] prior to engaging enemies.
* Maintain [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]] to keep your health up.
* Use [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] to reduce damage to 0 when necessary.

=== Against Groups of Charr ===
* Precast [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] and [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]], then run up to the casters (Dominators/Flameshielders).
* Charr Axemasters have [[gww:Bull's Strike|Bull's Strike]] so if there are any of those, let them hit you while stationary. The knockdown time from [[gww:Shield of Judgment|SoJ]] will be enough for you to run up to the casters without having to worry about getting KD'd.
* Auto-attack to build up adrenaline. Use [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] as necessary.
* Use [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]], [[gww:EBSoH|EBSoH]], and [[gww:Whirlwind Attack|Whirlwind Attack]] to spike.
* [[gww:Splinter Weapon|SW]] + [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]]/[[gww:Whirlwind Attack|Whirlwind Attack]] should to significant enough damage that [[gww:Shield of Judgment|SoJ]] and auto-attacking can clean up whatever is left.

=== Against Groups of Undead ===
* Precast [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] and [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]], then aggro the group.
* The casters (Ash Phantoms, Crypt Banshees, Shock Phantoms, Crypt Wraiths) will run away when you try and run up to them, so target the melee foes first (Crypt Slashers, Crypt Ghouls).
* The Ghouls have [[gww:Savage Slash|Savage Slash]], so be wary of that. Try to cast important skills while foes are knocked down from [[gww:Shield of Judgment|SoJ]].
* Auto-attack to build up adrenaline. Use [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] as necessary.
* Use [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]], [[gww:EBSoH|EBSoH]], and [[gww:Whirlwind Attack|Whirlwind Attack]] to spike.
* There will likely be one or two casters leftover from your spike. Auto-attacking with [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] will get rid of them easily.

=== Against Groups of Enchanted ===
* Precast [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] and [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]].
* Prior to engaging, make note of if there are any Enchanted Daggers, as they have [[gww:Disrupting Stab|Disrupting Stab]]. As with the Ghouls, cast important spells while they are knocked down and try to take them out first.
* Auto-attack to build up adrenaline. Use [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] as necessary.
* Use [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]], [[gww:EBSoH|EBSoH]], and [[gww:Whirlwind Attack|Whirlwind Attack]] to spike.
* Take care of remaining enemies with [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] + [[gww:EBSoH|EBSoH]].

=== Against [[gww:Faze Magekiller|Faze Magekiller]] ===
* Have your bonders pre-cast their enchantments on you, then go directly up to Faze.
* Auto-attack Faze while the melee enemies ball up around you.
* [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] spike as usual then auto-attack Faze until he is dead.
* If [[gww:Spell Breaker|Spell Breaker]] drops before Faze dies, make sure you are covering yourself with [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]] or [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] to avoid your more important enchantments form being removed.

=== Against [[gww:The Keeper|The Keeper]] ===
* Have your bonders pre-cast their enchantments on you, then go directly up to Faze.
* Auto-attack Faze while the melee enemies ball up around you.
* [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] spike as usual then auto-attack Faze until he is dead.
* If [[gww:Spell Breaker|Spell Breaker]] drops before Faze dies, make sure you are covering yourself with [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]] or [[gww:Shield of Absorption|Shield of Absorption]] to avoid your more important enchantments form being removed.

=== Against [[gww:Tyndir Flamecaller|Tyndir Flamecaller]] ===
* Same deal as regular Charr groups.
* Make sure to target [[gww:Tyndir Flamecaller|Tyndir Flamecaller]] first.

=== Against [[gww:Vraxx the Condemned|Vraxx the Condemned]] ===
* Precast all your regular enchantments, except for [[gww:Spell Breaker|Spell Breaker]], as his group is entirely melee.
* Ball them against the wall, and spike as usual. Make sure to target [[gww:Vraxx the Condemned|Vraxx]] first, as he has [[gww:Signet of Return|Signet of Return]] and will resurrect his allies.
* Clean up remainders by auto-attacking them.

=== Against [[gww:The Master|The Master]] ===
* Have your bonders pre-cast their enchantments on you. Precast [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] and [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]].
* Upon aggro, cast [[gww:Shield of Absorption|SoA]] and run directly up to [[gww:The Master|The Master]].
* [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] spike as usual.
* Be extra wary of when you have run out of hits for [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]], as [[gww:The Master|The Master]] is accompanied by a lot of enemies who will easily overwhelm you if you're not paying attention.

=== Against [[gww:Murakai's Steward|Murakai's Steward]] ===
* Prior to entering the room, have your bonders pre-cast their enchantments on you.
* When you run towards [[gww:Murakai's Steward|Murakai's Steward]], a dozen or so Undead enemies will pop up and attack you, so be sure to precast [[gww:Protective Spirit|Protective Spirit]] and [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]] before running up to him.
* Ingore the popups and run directly to [[gww:Murakai's Steward|Murakai's Steward]].
* Recast [[gww:Spirit Bond|Spirit Bond]] and cast [[gww:Shield of Absorption|SoA]].
* [[gww:Hundred Blades|100b]] spike as usual.
* Once [[gww:Murakai's Steward|Murakai's Steward]] is dead, grab the key and run back outside the chamber to lose extra aggro (or kill them if you want more Deldrimor points or loot).

=== Against [[gww:Murakai, Lady of the Night|Murakai, Lady of the Night]] ===
* Flag your heros far enough away to avoid aggro, but close enough that if you need them to recast enchantments on you they can do so.
* Have your bonders pre-cast their enchantments on you, except for [[gww:Shield of Judgment|SoJ]].
* Immediately when you aggro Murakai, she uses [[gww:Murakai's_Call|Murakai's Call]] which spawns a group of [[gww:Servant of Murakai|Servants of Murakai]]. Kill these, then pull Murakai onto a flame trap to help kill her faster.
* Run up to Murakai after pulling her onto the flame trap and attack her, using your skills as necessary to survive and deal more damage.
* Have your heros recast their enchantments on you to help you deal more damage. Be careful of when Murakai uses [[gww:Murakai's_Call|Murakai's Call]].
* Rinse and repeat until Murakai is dead.

== Notes ==
* It is important to keep note of which enemies you are facing, and which ones have knockdowns and interrupts. These can both be avoided by casting important skills while dangerous enemies are knocked down.
* Bonder 2 has [[gww:Dwayna's Kiss|Dwayna's Kiss]] and [[gww:Life Attunement|Life Attunement]] to keep Bonder 1 alive when facing [[gww:Crypt Banshee|Crypt Banshees]], which reflect damage with [[gww:Reversal of Damage|Reversal of Damage]].